      <div data-module="govspeak" class="gem-c-govspeak govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">
    
        <div class="govspeak"><p>You can view the disease surveillance analyses and data collected by the Animal and Plant Health Agency (<abbr title="Animal and Plant Health Agency">APHA</abbr>) to identify new or re-emerging threats to animal and public health.</p>

<p>Veterinary scanning surveillance at <abbr title="Animal and Plant Health Agency">APHA</abbr> is managed by the Surveillance Intelligence Unit (<abbr title="Surveillance Intelligence Unit">SIU</abbr>).</p>

<div class="call-to-action">
  <p>Read more about how <abbr title="Animal and Plant Health Agency">APHA</abbr>:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/guidance/animal-disease-scanning-surveillance-at-apha">carries out disease surveillance</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/information-on-data-analysis">analyses surveillance data</a></li>
  </ul>
</div>

<h2 id="monthly-surveillance-reports">Monthly surveillance reports</h2>

<p>The <abbr title="Surveillance Intelligence Unit">SIU</abbr> publishes <a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/apha-disease-surveillance-monthly-reports">monthly reports</a> on disease monitoring in livestock and poultry.</p>

<h2 id="focus-articles-published-in-journals">Focus articles published in journals</h2>

<p><abbr title="Animal and Plant Health Agency">APHA</abbr> publishes <a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/apha-animal-disease-surveillance-focus-articles">focus articles in Veterinary Record</a> which cover seasonal disease threats and emerging disease trends.</p>

<p>All articles are open access.</p>

<h2 id="quarterly-and-annual-species-reports">Quarterly and annual species reports</h2>

<p>The <abbr title="Surveillance Intelligence Unit">SIU</abbr> publishes periodic reports for livestock and wildlife covering:</p>

<ul>
  <li>new and re-emerging diseases and threats</li>
  <li>changes in disease patterns</li>
  <li>unusual diagnoses</li>
  <li>horizon scanning</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="equine-reports">Equine reports</h3>

<p>The Equine Quarterly Disease Surveillance report (<a rel="external" href="https://equinesurveillance.org/landing/"><abbr title="Equine Quarterly Disease Surveillance report">EIDS</abbr></a>) is produced in partnership with <abbr title="Animal and Plant Health Agency">APHA</abbr> and the British Equine Veterinary Association (<abbr title="British Equine Veterinary Association">BEVA</abbr>) and is published on the <abbr title="Equine Quarterly Disease Surveillance report">EIDS</abbr> website and in the Veterinary Record.</p>

<h3 id="livestock-reports">Livestock reports</h3>

<p>Read reports on:</p>

<ul>
  <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/avian-gb-disease-surveillance-and-emerging-threats-reports">avian surveillance and emerging threats</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/cattle-gb-disease-surveillance-and-emerging-threats-reports">cattle surveillance and emerging threats</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/exotic-and-farmed-species-gb-disease-surveillance-and-emerging-threats-reports">exotic and farmed species surveillance and emerging threats</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/pig-gb-disease-surveillance-and-emerging-threats-reports">pig surveillance and emerging threats</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/small-ruminant-gb-disease-surveillance-and-emerging-threats-reports">sheep and goats surveillance and emerging threats</a></li>
</ul>

<h3 id="wildlife-reports">Wildlife reports</h3>

<p>Read the report on <a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/wildlife-gb-disease-surveillance-and-emerging-threats-reports">wildlife surveillance and emerging threats</a>.</p>

<h3 id="small-animal-reports">Small animal reports</h3>

<p>Read the <a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/small-animal-expert-group-annual-summary">Small Animal Expert Group annual summary</a>.</p>

<h3 id="specialist-group-reports">Specialist group reports</h3>

<p>Read reports on:</p>

<ul>
  <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/chemical-food-safety-reports">chemical food safety in livestock</a></li>
  <li>parasitology
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/parasitology-literature-review-and-horizon-scanning">literature review and horizon scanning from the parasitology group</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/surveillance-reports-into-free-ectoparasite-examination-for-sheep-scab-in-wales">ectoparasite examination for sheep scab in Wales</a></li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/zoonoses-and-veterinary-public-health-disease-surveillance-reports">zoonoses and veterinary public health threat</a></li>
</ul>

<h2 id="information-notes">Information notes</h2>

<p>We publish <a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/disease-information-notes-from-apha">information notes</a> in response to circumstances where vets may require further guidance, such as:</p>

<ul>
  <li>unusual seasonal events</li>
  <li>emerging diseases</li>
  <li>outbreaks of non-statutory disease</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="vida-reports">
<abbr title="Veterinary Investigation Diagnosis Analysis">VIDA</abbr> reports</h2>

<p>The <abbr title="Surveillance Intelligence Unit">SIU</abbr> stores its data in the Veterinary Investigation Diagnosis Analysis (<abbr title="Veterinary Investigation Diagnosis Analysis">VIDA</abbr>) database.</p>

<p><abbr title="Veterinary Investigation Diagnosis Analysis">VIDA</abbr> contains records of every diagnostic submission from livestock and wildlife in Great Britain since 1975.</p>

<p>Since 2017, <abbr title="Animal and Plant Health Agency">APHA</abbr> has produced an annual <abbr title="Veterinary Investigation Diagnosis Analysis">VIDA</abbr> report on Tableau:</p>

<ul>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/siu.apha/viz/VIDAAnnualReport2025/VIDAAnnualReport2025"><abbr title="Veterinary Investigation Diagnosis Analysis">VIDA</abbr> report 2025</a></li>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/siu.apha/viz/VIDAAnnualReport2024/VIDAAnnualReport2024"><abbr title="Veterinary Investigation Diagnosis Analysis">VIDA</abbr> report 2024</a></li>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/siu.apha/viz/VIDAAnnualReport2023/VIDAAnnualReport2023"><abbr title="Veterinary Investigation Diagnosis Analysis">VIDA</abbr> report 2023</a></li>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/siu.apha/viz/VIDAAnnualReport2022/VIDAAnnualReport2022"><abbr title="Veterinary Investigation Diagnosis Analysis">VIDA</abbr> report 2022</a></li>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/siu.apha/viz/VIDAAnnualReport2021/VIDAAnnualReport2021"><abbr title="Veterinary Investigation Diagnosis Analysis">VIDA</abbr> report 2021</a></li>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/profile/siu.apha#!/vizhome/VIDAAnnualReport2020/VIDAAnnualReport2020"><abbr title="Veterinary Investigation Diagnosis Analysis">VIDA</abbr> report 2020</a></li>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/profile/siu.apha#!/vizhome/VIDAAnnualReport2019/VIDAAnnualReport2019"><abbr title="Veterinary Investigation Diagnosis Analysis">VIDA</abbr> report 2019</a></li>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/profile/siu.apha#!/vizhome/VIDAAnnualReport2018/VIDAAnnualReport2018"><abbr title="Veterinary Investigation Diagnosis Analysis">VIDA</abbr> report 2018</a></li>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/profile/siu.apha#!/vizhome/VIDAAnnualReport2017/VIDAAnnualReport2017"><abbr title="Veterinary Investigation Diagnosis Analysis">VIDA</abbr> report 2017</a></li>
</ul>

<p>You can access <a rel="external" href="https://webarchive.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ukgwa/20200807201619/https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/veterinary-investigation-diagnosis-analysis-vida-report/veterinary-investigation-diagnosis-analysis-vida-report">older annual <abbr title="Veterinary Investigation Diagnosis Analysis">VIDA</abbr> Reports</a> in the national archives.</p>

<h2 id="disease-surveillance-dashboards">Disease surveillance dashboards</h2>

<p>Animal disease surveillance data for Great Britain collected by <abbr title="Animal and Plant Health Agency">APHA</abbr> and Scotland’s Rural College (<abbr title="Scotland's Rural College">SRUC</abbr>).</p>

<p>Diagnoses are recorded for the month in which the submissions were received. The dashboards are updated on a monthly basis, adding all diagnoses allocated since the previous month’s update.</p>

<p>You can view each dashboard on Tableau:</p>

<ul>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/siu.apha/viz/AvianDashboard/Overview">avian disease</a></li>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/siu.apha/viz/CattleDashboard/Overview">cattle disease</a></li>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/siu.apha/viz/PigDashboard/Overview">pig disease</a></li>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/siu.apha/viz/SheepDashboard_/Overview">sheep disease</a></li>
</ul>

<h3 id="other-dashboards">Other dashboards</h3>

<ul>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/siu.apha/viz/BatRabiesDashboard/Intro">bat rabies</a></li>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/siu.apha/viz/BrachyspirahyodysenteriaeMLSTdashboard/Intro">Brachyspira hyodysenteriae isolate MLST in pigs</a></li>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/siu.apha/viz/Tick-bornediseasestory/TBD">tick-borne disease</a></li>
  <li><a rel="external" href="https://public.tableau.com/app/profile/siu.apha/viz/Porcinereproductiveandrespiratorysyndrome/PRRS">porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome</a></li>
</ul>

<h3 id="how-to-use-the-dashboards">How to use the dashboards</h3>

<p>To learn more about how to use the dashboards, see the <a rel="external" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y8gKSRLbAak">sheep disease surveillance dashboard video</a>. </p>

<p><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/siu-dashboards-data-limitations">Read more detailed information about the dashboards and their limitations</a>.</p>

<h2 id="livestock-population-reports-and-maps">Livestock population reports and maps</h2>

<p>View population density maps of farm animals in Great Britain published by the Livestock Demographic Data Group (<abbr title="Livestock Demographic Data Group">LDDG</abbr>).</p>

<p>You can view data and maps for the:</p>

<ul>
  <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/cattle-population-in-great-britain-annual-reports">cattle population</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/pig-population-in-great-britain-annual-reports">pig population</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/poultry-population-in-great-britain-annual-reports">poultry population</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/sheep-and-goat-population-in-great-britain-annual-reports">sheep and goat population</a></li>
</ul>

<h2 id="apha-science-blog">
<abbr title="Animal and Plant Health Agency">APHA</abbr> science blog</h2>

<p>Subscribe to the <a rel="external" href="https://aphascience.blog.gov.uk/"><abbr title="Animal and Plant Health Agency">APHA</abbr> science blog</a> with news and updates from <abbr title="Animal and Plant Health Agency">APHA</abbr>.</p>

<h2 id="videos">Videos</h2>

<p><abbr title="Animal and Plant Health Agency">APHA</abbr> produces and publishes videos on its <a rel="external" href="https://www.youtube.com/c/APHAgov">YouTube channel</a>.</p>

<p>You can also watch our:</p>

<ul>
  <li>
<a rel="external" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y8gKSRLbAak&amp;list=PLouExecY1KnerHD5nwYRx3baUYxGdIJxx">animal disease surveillance</a> playlist</li>
  <li>
<a rel="external" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K-80PfO2KQQ&amp;list=PLouExecY1KnffE86A0Swih5UbnNW-1WMD">Surveillance Intelligence forum 2023</a> playlist</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="alerts">Alerts</h2>

<p><abbr title="Animal and Plant Health Agency">APHA</abbr> has 3 alert systems for vets:</p>

<ul>
  <li><a href="https://www.gov.uk/guidance/apha-alert-subscription-service">exotic notifiable diseases</a></li>
  <li>
<a href="https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sign-up-for-apha-disease-alerts-for-vets">Endemic and Emerging Disease Alert System (EEDAS)</a> for farmed animals</li>
  <li>
<a href="https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sign-up-for-apha-disease-alerts-for-vets">SmART (Small Animal Risks and Threats)</a> </li>
</ul>

</div>

</div>
      
